+
+The target was 10 km. The pass reached 7.64 km because the remaining large candidates could not be dated with this series. Flygfältsvägen and northern Möckelövägen lie west of the 1968–1985 sheet frame. Uppgårdsvägen, Vikingagränd, Lövdalsvägen, Blomstringevägen, Örnvägen and Falkvägen are missing or unclear up to 1995. They were left undated rather than stretched.
+
+## Findings for the four follow-ups
+
+**Godbyvägen at Strandnäs.** In 1968, Godbyvägen ran straight south to a four-way crossing with the straight Sjukhusvägen–Lemlandsvägen. The 1978 red overprint adds Rökerirondellen and a diagonal connector, while the old crossing remains in the base drawing. By 1985 the straight approach has gone, apart from a southern stub that survives today as a cul-de-sac (way 34984271). That stub keeps the old approach's identity: it shows the 1968 trace geometry for 1968–1984 and the modern stub from 1985. The straight through-route has the state *abandoned* from 1985, the first edition without it, so no demolition year is assumed. Modern approaches are not backdated to 1968.
+
+**Nya Godbyvägen north.** The 1978 overprint joins Godbyvägen further north on a different line, so it is recorded as unclear and not used for geometry. In 1985 the road curves north-east into Godbyvägen at the node between ways 77082297 and 166080070. That curve no longer exists. It has been traced from the 1985 scan and is shown for 1985–1994. Way 70750975 shows only its southern part, up to the branch point, for 1978–1994 (partial coverage). From 1995 it shows the full modern line, and the straight northern continuation starts in 1995. The little roundabout at Michaelsvägen is later than 1995 and stays undated. The 1995 link to Godbyvägen is a footway/cycleway today, so it is deferred.
+
+**Åsvägen and northern Ålandsvägen.** In 1968 and 1978, only contours, plot boundaries and a short yard lane appear on Åsvägen's line; none of these is backdated. Åsvägen is first drawn as a street in 1985. The street north of Ålandsvägen's roundabout is a double-lined street on every edition from 1968. The parallel street to its east first appears in 1995 and stays separate.
+
+**Roundabouts and approaches.** Rökerirondellen is dated 1978. Västra rondellen is dated 1995, replacing a Y-junction. Each ring is its own object, separate from its approach legs, and the legs carry their own dates. Channelised junctions not visible by 1995 stay undated: Nya Godbyvägen/Bolstavägen, Godbyvägen/Bolstavägen and Michaelsvägen.
+
+## Method and data
+
+Original-scan crops for each area and edition, with overlays, sequences and crop metadata (bbox, pixel box, scan SHA-256), are in `data/map-scan-cache/review/mariehamn-major-roads/followups/`. Every section was visually compared across all four editions; overlays were only aids. `crop.py` and `trace.py` produced the crops and the centre-line samples.
+
+`data/mariehamn-major-road-followups.json` is generated by `followups/prepare.py`. That script captures input hashes and is kept for audit, so do not rerun it blindly. The file holds:
+
+- exact modern members, their city-stage links and the 2014/2021/2025 originals with the same OSM id (missing years are explicit);
+- per-edition observations (present, absent or unclear, with full, partial or unknown coverage);
+- explicit state and geometry periods;
+- for the three vanished or realigned lines: the raw scan trace (accepted and rejected samples, crop and hash) and a reconstructed line anchored to modern junction nodes.
+
+`scripts/mariehamn_major_road_followups.py` runs after the first pass. It validates everything before any change is made to the catalogue:
+
+- input hashes;
+- single ownership of each source;
+- continuity of the sections;
+- trace deviation of at most 25 m, and anchors within 1 m of the modern junctions;
+- partial extents that equal a substring of the modern road;
+- removal only at the first edition without the road;
+- counted lengths.
+
+Raw traces and unmodified modern and original geometries are preserved as evidence. All matching happens at build time.
+
+Deferred items are listed in the review file. They include:
+
+- Lemlandsvägen's 40 m at the old crossing. Its rural object starts in 1985 and needs splitting before it can be backdated, so a gap remains for 1968–1984 rather than a duplicate identity.
+- The road running south from the old crossing.
+- The old Y-junction at Västra rondellen.
+- Vedhuggsvägen's middle 53 m, which is now a cycleway.
+- The second carriageway of Västra Utfarten and the southern bend of Klintvägen.
+
+## Validation
+
+The catalogue at the start of the pass (`followups/before.json.gz`) was 36,025 objects. Other uncommitted work had already changed `data/rural-map-review.json`, adding nine 1968 Yttern building decisions and changing 19 buildings. A rebuild from the current sources therefore gives 36,034 objects even with this pass disabled. `followups/audit.py` rebuilds that baseline and compares it with the new catalogue: 36,034 → 36,071 objects and 45,816 → 46,157 geometries. All 37 added objects are the reviewed ones and all 341 added geometries carry this pass's prefix. No existing object, geometry or city stage changed, and no source gained a second owner. The unrelated snapshot-to-baseline difference is recorded separately in `followups/scope-audit.json`.
+
+`tests/mariehamn-major-road-followups.test.cjs` checks:
+
+- first visibility and absence before each first year;
+- per-edition evidence;
+- stable modern geometry 2014–2026;
+- single ownership;
+- the reconstructed Strandnäs crossing and its connection to Sjukhusvägen;
+- the 1985 curve's joins to way 70750975 and Godbyvägen;
+- the partial-to-full change in 1995;
+- separate roundabout dates;
+- preserved traces;
+- deferred ways remaining unowned;
+- the first-pass start dates.
+
+`tests/test_mariehamn_major_road_followups.py` checks that changed traces, unanchored lines, removals without an absent edition, early starts, altered partial extents, double ownership and changed inputs are all rejected without touching the catalogue.
+
+Two assertions in `tests/temporal-objects.test.cjs` changed because of this pass: the global identity count now includes the 37 objects, and the Österleden ramps at Rökerirondellen now belong to their dated approach object. All 455 JavaScript tests pass. The loader's recent-changes note is updated and cache versions are refreshed.
+
+Deployed on 2026-11-11 with Wrangler as version `82982643-8c44-41dd-8842-a69babacd39c`. All 455 JavaScript tests passed and the dry run was clean before publication. Seven live files match local SHA-256 hashes, including the page, object page, catalogue and review data, and the live catalogue contains all 37 follow-up objects with the expected states. The published catalogue also includes the unrelated, already-present `rural-map-review.json` changes. See `followups/deployment.json`.
